Subject: [PATCH] build: build vtest without vrend

Since "build: Add vrend option to allow Vulkan-only builds" (06960f84), -Dvrend=false builds
virglrenderer without libepoxy and the OpenGL renderer, but it also skips vtest, so a
Venus-only vtest server cannot be built. vtest needs nothing of vrend: it uses the public
virglrenderer API, the copied Mesa util code (src/mesa/util) and, when found, libdrm; its
gallium_dep is the not-found dependency that src/meson.build sets without vrend. Without
vrend the server runs with --venus --no-virgl only.

Written from virglrenderer e18f8c00 meson.build, vtest/meson.build and src/meson.build.

---
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -489,7 +489,7 @@
 endif

 subdir('src')
-if with_vrend and not with_host_windows
+if not with_host_windows
    subdir('vtest')
 endif

